# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# Mustfile — Physical-state contract for progblocks
# Author: Jonathan D.A. Jewell (hyperpolymath)
#
# What MUST be true about this repository. Hard requirements. Several of
# these ARE mechanically enforced (by ci.yml / codeql.yml / secret-scanner.yml
# on every push); others are documentary until something automates them —
# each entry says which.

@abstract:
Physical-state invariants for progblocks, a pre-alpha, dependency-free web
component with no runtime dependencies. Probes target this repository's
real tree, not a generic template.
@end

## File Presence

### license-present
- description: LICENSE file must exist and be the canonical MPL-2.0 text
- run: test -f LICENSE && grep -q 'Mozilla Public License Version 2.0' LICENSE
- severity: critical
- enforced-by: not yet automated (documentary)

### readme-present
- description: README.md must exist (this repo keeps README as .md, a logged deviation — see ../rsr-profile.a2ml)
- run: test -f README.md
- severity: critical
- enforced-by: not yet automated (documentary)

### security-policy
- description: SECURITY.md must exist
- run: test -f SECURITY.md
- severity: critical
- enforced-by: not yet automated (documentary)

### governance-docs
- description: GOVERNANCE.md and .github/CODEOWNERS must exist
- run: test -f GOVERNANCE.md && test -f .github/CODEOWNERS
- severity: critical
- enforced-by: not yet automated (documentary)

### ai-manifest
- description: 0-AI-MANIFEST.a2ml must exist at the repository root
- run: test -f 0-AI-MANIFEST.a2ml
- severity: critical
- enforced-by: not yet automated (documentary)

## The component itself

### component-source-present
- description: The <prog-block> custom element source file must exist and define the element
- run: test -f src/prog-block.js && grep -q "customElements.define('prog-block'" src/prog-block.js
- severity: critical
- enforced-by: not yet automated (documentary) — defining the call is necessary but not sufficient; see contractiles/bust/Bustfile.a2ml's component-fails-to-register for why the module can still fail to load

### demo-page-present
- description: index.html must exist and reference the component
- run: test -f index.html && grep -q 'prog-block' index.html
- severity: critical
- enforced-by: not yet automated (documentary)

### test-suite-present
- description: At least one node:test file must exist under tests/
- run: test -n "$(find tests -name '*.test.js' 2>/dev/null)"
- severity: critical
- enforced-by: ci.yml `build` job (via `just test`) — though see contractiles/dust/Dustfile.a2ml for why a green run here is not currently trustworthy

## CI / lockfile

### actions-lockfile-present
- description: The gh actions-lock lockfile must exist
- run: test -f .github/workflows/actions.lock
- severity: critical
- enforced-by: not yet automated (documentary) — do not "fix" uses: lines in the workflow files back to inline SHAs; the lockfile is the pin

## Directory structure

### machine-readable-dir
- description: .machine_readable/ directory must exist, with descriptiles + contractiles + rsr-profile.a2ml
- run: test -d .machine_readable/descriptiles && test -d .machine_readable/contractiles && test -f .machine_readable/rsr-profile.a2ml
- severity: critical
- enforced-by: not yet automated (documentary)

### well-known-present
- description: The .well-known trio exists
- run: test -f .well-known/ai.txt && test -f .well-known/humans.txt && test -f .well-known/security.txt
- severity: warning
- enforced-by: not yet automated (documentary)

## Template integrity

### a2ml-spdx-headers
- description: Every .a2ml file this pass created carries an SPDX identifier on line 1
- run: test $(find . -name '*.a2ml' -not -path './node_modules/*' -not -path './.git/*' -exec sh -c 'head -1 $1 | grep -q SPDX-License-Identifier: || echo BAD' _ {} ';' | wc -l) -eq 0
- severity: critical
- enforced-by: not yet automated (documentary) — as of 2026-08-07 this probe currently FAILS for two pre-existing files outside this sweep's scope, .github/DISCUSSION_TEMPLATE/0.2-AI-MANIFEST.a2ml and .github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/0.2-AI-MANIFEST.a2ml, neither of which carries an SPDX header at all; fixing those is a separate task, not silently expanded into here

## No verification ledger to check

This repo has no VERIFICATION.md and no src/verify*.mjs scripts, and makes
no formal proof claims — see ../descriptiles/NEUROSYM.a2ml. contracts.ncl
and package.k9 describe intent; nothing in this tree consumes them.
